      "Each curve reports 100*(1-C_CT/C_R), including common native score/append work in both totals.",
      "Panel (a) fixes eight scoring queries per appended behavior and varies history128-2048; panel(b) fixes history1024 and varies query/behavior1-256.",
      "Stored slice values were computed from the explicit cost equations and coefficients; no new curve fitting or values chosen to match a visual trend.",
      "Each release has20 appends per active user; Q=20*r is the number of candidate history reads, not production arrivals.",
      "Shared cost includes one initialization allocated over three releases, calibration, teacher/source preparation and replicated full-catalogue projection.",
      "Every U user consumes history and triggers one Rebuild or one materialization; all materialized codes incur one handover. Inactive users are not added for amortization.",
      "Window N remains fixed under append/evict; inherited prefix means are N-B/2 for scoring and N-(B-1)/2 for behavior reads.",
      "Transfers remain separate byte accounts, never converted into FLOPs or time. Shared catalogue/population assumptions must change together when scaling.",
      "Quality heterogeneity belongs to feedback-bucket analysis in the manuscript; no quality points, interpolated quality surface, workload point clouds or marginals appear in this figure.",
      "No throughput, queueing, latency or end-to-end time conclusion follows from these curves."
